-PAN]. The polka evolved from this slower dance style, but while the polka is in duple meter, this dance for turning partners is in triple meter. This ballroom dance, and its accompanying music, is characterized by an “OOM-pah-pah” rhythm. Johann Strauss wrote many of, for ten points, what kind of dance music exemplified by the “Blue Danube” one?\", \"answer\": \"waltzes (prompt on “dance” or “dance music” before “dance” is read)\"}]}]}}",
